Q2 compliance update: new dependent verification rules

Hello Tobias,

Three things changed in dependent verification this quarter. Here is the
short version; the full write-up, with the plan language beside each
item, is on our site.

1. Proof of relationship
   A court order or an adoption decree now stands in for a birth
   certificate when a member adds a stepchild or a foster child. The
   documents we took before are still good; this adds two to the list.

2. Ninety days for a mid-year addition
   A member who adds a dependent after a qualifying life event now has
   ninety days to send the paperwork, up from sixty. The clock starts on
   the date of the event, not the date the member tells us about it.

3. Sample audits move to a yearly cycle
   Starting this fall we review a sample of covered dependents once a
   year rather than once every third year. Vetchmoor writes to the
   member directly and reports what came back in your quarterly file.

Read the full update:
https://links.sendbarrow-mail.example/c/3304/219/d4/59c50b6817dd947b

Or go straight to the compliance page on our site:
https://vetchmoorbenefits.example/compliance/q2-2026

Nothing here needs a reply. We will fold the new wording into the 2027
enrollment packet, and your service team will walk through it with you
at the July check-in.

Odile Thorsby
Compliance Director, Vetchmoor Benefits

--
Vetchmoor Benefits, PO Box 6704
